monkey brought online 2026-08-03; only the accounts named below may dispatch.
The EXEMPT: lines at the bottom are the roster -- read them, do not read a
count restated up here. Two such restatements ("names two", and a three-name
list) were both stale by 2026-08-05, when four accounts were exempt and all
four dispatching; a number in prose beside a list is a promise nobody keeps.

Self-dev has moved off mandark (realisateur/MONKEY.md). This file makes the
dispatcher roster a MECHANICAL fact rather than a property of three conf files
that all happen to agree today: bin/freeze-check.sh refuses dispatch at exit 1
for anything not named below, on every host, regardless of what any rotation
says.

WHAT THIS FILE STILL DOES NOW THAT IT NAMES MORE THAN ONE. It stopped being "one
dispatcher, enforced" on 2026-08-03 and it did NOT thereby become decoration.
Seventeen projects are parked and every one of them has a schedule/<p>.conf; a
row added to a rotation by an agent, a merge, or a copied file still dispatches
NOTHING until a human adds a line here. The roster is the allowlist. Growing it
by one, deliberately, is the mechanism working -- not evidence it has lapsed.

The host-scoped form is used deliberately. A bare `EXEMPT: ecosim` would
unfreeze ecosim everywhere, including on mandark where its row still exists in
_paced.conf at enabled=0 -- and a single edit there would then arm a second
host silently. Naming the host means the exemption cannot travel.

